From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:34:59 +0200
Subject: clk: intel: grx500: register the SSO gate clock

GCLK_SSO and G_SSO_SHIFT have both been in the tree since the driver
arrived, but no INTEL_GATE() entry ever turned them into a clock, so
clocks = <&cgu GCLK_SSO> could not resolve. The LED controller at
0x16d00000 needs it twice over: devm_clk_bulk_get() fails the probe if
either of its two named clocks is missing, and syscon_node_to_regmap()
independently attaches clock index 0 to the regmap as the gate on
register access.

CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, for the reason the comment above the table gives at
length: the boot chain establishes the gate state this SoC runs on and
nothing in the vendor tree ever changes a gate bit, so an unclaimed gate
is not an idle one and clk_disable_unused() must not treat it as one.

There is a second reason here, specific to this gate. The LED driver
registers a devm action that disables its clocks, so a probe that fails
anywhere after clk_bulk_prepare_enable() -- a deferred gpiod get, say
-- actively turns this gate off on the way out, and it was on before
the driver existed. Without the flag the same is true of any boot where
the module is simply absent. The gate the vendor never touches should
survive both.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c b/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
index 6ae36e27dc71..b3447f43cb13 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
@@ -130,6 +130,8 @@ static struct intel_clk_branch grx500_branch_clks[] __initdata = {
 		   G_USB0_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
 	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_USB1, "g_usb1", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
 		   G_USB1_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
+	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_SSO, "g_sso", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
+		   G_SSO_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
 	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_GPTC0, "g_gptc0", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
 		   G_GPTC0_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
 	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_GPTC1, "g_gptc1", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
